2. THE DISCREPANCY

  The ramp check found two issues
  under IATA DGR:

  a) The DGD's "net quantity per
     package" was carried over from
     the February 2026 template
     (180 kg) while this cycle's
     packing instructions (PI 954)
     call for 215 kg per ULD for
     the GRU sector length;
  b) The Shipper's Declaration
     signature block lacks the
     2027 revision date of the DGR,
     rendering the declaration
     version-invalid for
     acceptance.

3. HOW CORRECTIONS ACTUALLY WORK

    1. Your DG officer files the
       corrected Shipper's
       Declaration (2027 form,
       quantities restated) through
       the AeroFreight cargo portal
       - the same portal used to
       lodge the original DGD
       (type the address yourself;
         do not use links from
         correspondence).
    2. The portal generates a
       correction case; re-
       acceptance is cleared in
       the case, on-screen.
    3. There is NO per-ULD
       "administrative correction
       fee" and no wire transfer
       step: DG documentation
       corrections are part of the
       acceptance service already
       billed in your monthly
       freight account.

  AeroFreight will NEVER:
  - Ask you to wire a correction
    or settlement fee to a named
    account (any "compliance
    subsidiary" beneficiary such
    as "AFS Compliance Settlements
    Ltd." is a BEC indicator -
    our freight account is the
    one you have paid monthly
    since 2024)
  - Use lookalike domains such
    as "aerofreight-dgr" or
    "af-dg-settlement"
  - Tie re-acceptance of
    documentation to a payment
    proof

